;; The program that runs the gateway and serves its tools to an agent.
;;
;; The component is the checked part and this is the trusted part: what the
;; component may ask for is in its binary, and what it actually gets is this
;; program's doing. It is fetched rather than built here — a Rust program
;; embedding wasmtime, pinned by the hash beside its package — and its
;; source is in this pack under host/.
;;
;; It listens on the WireGuard address, which is why this feature is worth
;; composing onto the VPN appliance rather than onto any image with a
;; network: wg0 exists only after a peer with the right key has handshaked,
;; so reachability is the authentication MCP does not have of its own.

(fragment feature:agent-gateway-host

  (doc "Serves the gateway component's tools over MCP, on the VPN address")

  (requires
    (capability systemd-init)
    (capability no-console-login))

  (buildroot
    (y BR2_PACKAGE_AGENT_GATEWAY_HOST)

    ;; Its own overlay, not the component's. They were one directory until
    ;; it became clear that an image with the component and without this
    ;; feature would ship a unit whose binary is not installed, and fail at
    ;; boot for a reason nothing in the image explains.
    (path-append BR2_ROOTFS_OVERLAY "files-host")))
